# PostgreSQL

Apply this rule when work touches the PostgreSQL service, schema, migrations,
or database configuration.

## Schema conventions

- Tables: `snake_case`, plural (`users`, `order_items`)
- Columns: `snake_case` (`created_at`, `user_id`)
- Indexes: `idx_<table>_<column(s)>`
- Primary keys: `pk_<table>`
- Unique constraints: `uq_<table>_<column(s)>`
- Foreign keys: `fk_<table>_<reference>`
- Check constraints: `chk_<table>_<rule>`

## Standard columns

Every table should include:

- `id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()`
- `created_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()`
- `updated_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()`
- `deleted_at timestamptz NULL` — only when soft delete is required

## Preferred types

| Concept | PG type |
|---------|---------|
| ID | `uuid` |
| Short text | `varchar(n)` |
| Long text | `text` |
| Boolean | `boolean` |
| Date/time | `timestamptz` |
| Money / decimals | `numeric(p, s)` — never `float` or `double precision` |
| JSON | `jsonb` |

## Foreign keys

- Always define explicit `ON DELETE` and `ON UPDATE` behavior — never rely on defaults
- Parent/owned records: `ON DELETE CASCADE` (e.g. order_items → orders)
- Reference/lookup records: `ON DELETE RESTRICT` or `SET NULL`
- Index every foreign key column

## Best practices

- Always use `timestamptz` for dates (not `timestamp` without timezone)
- Prefer `jsonb` over `json`
- Add indexes on search/filter columns and foreign keys
- Use partial indexes when filtering on a subset (e.g. `WHERE deleted_at IS NULL`)
- Avoid PostgreSQL enums for evolving domains — prefer `varchar` + check constraint or lookup tables
- Never edit applied migrations — create a new migration instead
- Configure via `.env` variables (`POSTGRES_HOST`, `POSTGRES_PORT`,
  `POSTGRES_USER`, `POSTGRES_PASSWORD`, `POSTGRES_DB`)

## Query guidelines

- Select only required columns — avoid `SELECT *` in application code
- Use parameterized queries (TypeORM handles this by default)
- Paginate large result sets (`LIMIT` / `OFFSET` or keyset pagination)
